From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: add an HEVC encoder component

Add c2.v4l2.hevc.encoder, enabled through
ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.encoder.supported.hevc like the other encoders.

- HEVC.{h,cpp}: Main tier level limits (H.265 Tables A.8 and A.9: maximum
  luma picture size, luma sample rate and bitrate, plus the A.4.1 bound of
  sqrt(8 * MaxLumaPs) on each dimension), the C2 to V4L2 level mapping,
  VPS/SPS/PPS extraction for the codec-specific data, and insertion of
  the cached parameter sets before IRAP pictures (IDR, CRA) that come
  without them.
- EncodeInterface: HEVC profile and level parameter. Only Main is
  offered: the input is 8-bit 4:2:0 (NV12), Main Still Picture allows a
  single picture per stream, and Main 10 needs a 10-bit input format.
  Levels 1 to 5.2, default 4.1. The setter mirrors the H.264 one: it
  keeps the requested level when that covers the size, frame rate and
  bitrate, and otherwise moves to the lowest level that does.
- EncodeComponent: HEVC codec-specific data (VPS, SPS and PPS) and the
  frame rate limit of the configured level.
- V4L2Encoder: the HEVC profile is required; level, B-frames, maximum QP
  and header mode are optional and set one at a time, so that a control
  the device lacks does not reject the others. The parameter sets go
  before each IRAP picture through
  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR when the device exposes it,
  otherwise the encoder inserts the cached ones, as it already does for
  H.264 (the Qualcomm iris gen1 encoder has no such control).

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
